---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../site.config';
---

<Base title="About" description="About Swaying Branches, the blog of Edward Ringler." section="about">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>About</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="prose about">
      <p><em>Swaying Branches</em> is the blog of {SITE.author}, written between 2013 and 2022.</p>
      <p>
        The name comes from his post <a href="/2013/11/swaying-branches.html">Swaying Branches</a>, about watching
        the trees from his front porch in Squirrel Hill.
      </p>
      <p>
        The posts were originally published at <a href={SITE.originalBlog}>swaying-branches.blogspot.com</a> and have
        been preserved here with his words unchanged. Each post keeps its original address, and links back to the
        original on Blogspot.
      </p>

      <h2 id="summaries">About the summaries</h2>
      <p>
        To help readers find their way around, each post has a one-line summary, a slightly longer summary at the top of
        the post, and a topic. These were written with the help of AI, from the text of each post, and describe what he
        wrote without adding to it. They are clearly marked, and each one says whether a family member has reviewed it
        yet.
      </p>
      <p>
        The summaries are only a guide. His own text, below each summary, is exactly as he published it: no words have
        been changed, added or removed. Where a summary and the post differ, the post is what he said.
      </p>
      <p>
        Search covers the full text of every post and ranks his own words above the summaries.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
